":238,"char_start":0,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5c0a661b00acb5dc","document_char_end":21236,"document_char_start":20998,"evidence_id":"ev_f5d376cf45523064","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"During the charge/discharge cycling of different battery samples, occasional noise can be observed in the 1st and 2nd cycles (Supporting information, Fig. S1 and S2), which originated from the lack of cell resting time before experiments.","source_sha256":"002de8ac949a05a331a2b07ea3e88a9e1ae236279cb1f37c24b936b45dffbb98"},{"char_end":863,"char_start":685,"chunk_id":"mdchk_5c0a661b00acb5dc","document_char_end":21861,"document_char_start":21683,"evidence_id":"ev_029f5e99c8de9c62","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"it should be noted that battery sample number 4 experienced a short-circuit during the 3rd discharge process. Therefore, this battery sample was excluded from further evaluation.","source_sha256":"002de8ac949a05a331a2b07ea3e88a9e1ae236279cb1f37c24b936b45dffbb98"},{"char_end":1288,"char_start":1220,"chunk_id":"mdchk_7cc1095fafb934bf","document_char_end":24878,"document_char_start":24810,"evidence_id":"ev_b66175428208d6e9","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"Notable is that the electrode coatings are manually prepared and are","source_sha256":"a011dd0f3e7b699dfb28e45ec0510e5b7953a940ca28212e61a4aeeeff277aba"},{"char_end":612,"char_start":420,"chunk_id":"mdchk_92689ed95586b62e","document_char_end":8944,"document_char_start":8752,"evidence_id":"ev_01e17d2905590a4c","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The Eioneus system consists of a platform with coin cell mounting and supply area, crimping and decrimping stations, a potentiostat-based electrochemical evaluation station and a control board","source_sha256":"765e465db86fd73981973ec888ea31fbc51d888035f3ed113875f6d59d27f55a"},{"char_end":347,"char_start":188,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":11246,"document_char_start":11087,"evidence_id":"ev_6e5fe4a9a0b0abe5","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"the robotic system starts the fully automated screening cycle. Bar-coded reaction vessels are checked in and fed to the Proteus robot conveyor in tube rackets.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":919,"char_start":657,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":11818,"document_char_start":11556,"evidence_id":"ev_aefbd055a875783e","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"the Proteus system moves the reaction vessels to the sampling preparation superblock, where it starts to dispense the correct volumes of the pre-mixed stock solutions of A and B. Before dispensing the stock solutions, the test tubes are purged with nitrogen gas.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1032,"char_start":932,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":11931,"document_char_start":11831,"evidence_id":"ev_5adedaa366fd1cc2","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"the solutions of A and B are mixed by stirring for a pre-defined time, which was set to about 1 min.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1233,"char_start":1033,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12132,"document_char_start":11932,"evidence_id":"ev_6c79086bf0b88221","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"An analytical chain, utilizing turbidity, controls if a precipitate has formed or not. If precipitation occurs, the screening cycle proceeds with addition of more solvent and repeated turbidity check.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1399,"char_start":1234,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12298,"document_char_start":12133,"evidence_id":"ev_0a244585992a95ab","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"If no precipitation can be detected, the analytical sequence continues to the next step involving Raman spec troscopy for characterisation of the electrolyte system.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1600,"char_start":1400,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12499,"document_char_start":12299,"evidence_id":"ev_66bd4aa647589196","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"Subsequently, sampling of 100 μL, 50 μL and 10 μL of the reaction solution is performed onto a 96-well plate at three different positions for further characteri sation, crystallisation and evaluation.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":1896,"char_start":1707,"chunk_id":"mdchk_b941c6f24fc3bb41","document_char_end":12795,"document_char_start":12606,"evidence_id":"ev_1d09d84d31dbe0ab","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"Our initial investigations show that 50 μL is an appropriate electrolyte vol ume. The electrolyte is dispensed directly onto the anode on the half coin cell prepared by the Eioneus systems.","source_sha256":"728064f55fc3b9a4f4c209dfc765a350ec05467093090c7777c73a323dac8cd3"},{"char_end":183,"char_start":46,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":28978,"document_char_start":28841,"evidence_id":"ev_c8fc1d45c925b229","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The electrode materials Li[Mn2O4] (LMO) and V2O5were provided by Sigma Aldrich and used as an active material without further treat ment.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":556,"char_start":432,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29351,"document_char_start":29227,"evidence_id":"ev_fbd6a1b349eed5a6","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"A viscous slurry was prepared as follows, a small amount of NMP was added and afterwards pasted onto a stainless-steel foil.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":556,"char_start":474,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29351,"document_char_start":29269,"evidence_id":"ev_abb758a0a131289f","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"a small amount of NMP was added and afterwards pasted onto a stainless-steel foil.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":619,"char_start":557,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29414,"document_char_start":29352,"evidence_id":"ev_33a2aac8f979ef92","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The prepared electrodes were dried in vacuum at 70◦C for 12 h.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":680,"char_start":620,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29475,"document_char_start":29415,"evidence_id":"ev_483172eb67713674","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The disc electrodes were punched out in a diameter of 13 mm.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":818,"char_start":742,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29613,"document_char_start":29537,"evidence_id":"ev_3e19ffe7f8fb2117","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The used separator was a Whatman glass fiber GF/A, with a diameter of 16 mm.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":880,"char_start":819,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29675,"document_char_start":29614,"evidence_id":"ev_e35ff3f63d52ea99","paper_id":"DOI:10.1016_j.cej.2022.140955","quote":"The full coin cell was assembled as a CR 2030-type coin cell.","source_sha256":"a75b4c4f315f4d5a50ad9a73a6c66ef30fcbe02f7a26585bfaf49520545382b1"},{"char_end":1135,"char_start":881,"chunk_id":"mdchk_d5ed12b60892cb04","document_char_end":29930,"document